## Domain
Audio as a prism domain. A synth patch IS a bigraph — module = a `process` with signal
ports, patch cable = a link, voice = a composite — so generative synthesis = a **BRS
rewriting that bigraph**. The AUDIBLE twin of quantum in the one-engine thesis. Code:
`crates/prism-audio` + `../gorgon` (the realtime audio/CV/ring library, folded in as a
lib). DSP kernels are native (Rust); `.ys`/Rust specs are the THIN layer — never clone
prism's BRS / engine / schema algebra. Adjacent agents: `unify` (the `functor` definer +
the shared `Complex`/`Signal[ℂ]` sort that make cross-domain audio natural), `manifold`
(the audio twin of the same M/R closure; shares the ℂ sort + the mesh binding), `mesh`
(the A8 transport), `core` (#15 schema-as-state, for InsertFilter), `lang` (the `.ys`
patch/reaction surface).

